okay so the attack on Titan manga was  published for over a decade and during  that time there's one specific panel  that's become more Infamous than  anything else as of making this video  there have been countless memes fan  animations and even a whole subreddit  with thousands of members dedicated to  this one particular scene in case you  have no idea what I'm talking about in  the final chapter of Attack on Titan  Aaron and Armin have a heartfelt  conversation about Mikasa during this  exchange Armin wonders if she'll ever be  able to move on with her life and find  her boyfriend or husband after Aaron  dies and in response to this Aaron loses  his mind and throws a tantrum inside the  paws Dimension with tears in his eyes he  tells Armin no I don't want that I want  her to think about me and no one else  for the rest of our life Mikasa finding  another man Even after I die I want her  to be hung up on me for a while 10 years  at least as you'd expect it didn't take  long for this to ironically become one  of Aaron's most memorable quotes in  particular the first line and the last  line to many people the wording here  just didn't sound like something you  would say and even Armin was surprised  by just how pathetic it was that's why  today we're about to explain the truth  about this moment specifically does it  detract from Aaron's character or was it  a perfectly reasonable thing to include  throughout this video I'll be as Fair as  I can to the two different perspectives  and at the end I'll tell you how my own  opinion has changed in the time since  the chapter was released alright so the  first place we need to start is with  isayama himself who actually spoke about  this scene during an interview last year  in that interview he said the idea  suddenly came to him as he was drawing  the Final Chapter because in his words  he's always loved whiny Aaron for that  reason this segment was him trying to  take the character back to his roots and  he even thought to himself Aaron is back  once he'd finished drawing it now  whether you love this panel or hate it I  think we can all agree that Aaron has  had a ton of emotional outbursts over  the years and so the whiny errand that  isayama is referring to isn't anything  new as an example there was the time he  couldn't work out how to use the odm  gear the time he broke down in front of  Ramsay all the time he straight up asked  Historia to kill him and you can see how  his behavior in scenes like this laid  the foundation for this oh obviously  there are differences that we'll be  talking about later but for now we need  to acknowledge that Aaron has never been  afraid of showing emotional  vulnerability bearing that in mind his  outburster Armin was not only perfectly  in line with his core character but it  was also a way for isayama to  demonstrate how repressed Aaron has been  from the moment he kissed his story his  hand and saw the future he wasn't  allowed to tell anyone what he knew or  Express his true feelings about it even  though he probably wanted to his  horrified face at the meadow ceremony  was the closest anyone got to seeing his  real emotions but for pretty much the  entire time after that he kept his  secrets to himself this extreme  isolation is something Armin  acknowledges in the Final Chapter and it  means Aaron's tantrum in parse was  actually four years worth of repressed  feelings coming to the surface during  those four tragic years he failed at  finding an alternative to the rumbling  he failed at keeping all of his friends  alive his one attempt at romance didn't  work and the founding Titan made him  kill his own mother on top of that he  knew he was destined to die no matter  what happened which would be a huge  mental burden for anyone let alone a 19  year old considering all of that his  emotions in the Final Chapter shouldn't  be as controversial as it is but what's  clear is that the timeskip distorted our  view of who he is as a character what I  mean is that when season 4 came around  we were introduced to an older version  of Aaron who was manipulative ruthless  and seemingly willing to put his friends  in danger based on his actions it was  easy to assume that Aaron had  organically turned into this person  during the four-year time skip however  now that we have all the facts we can  see that for most of the time skip he  didn't act like this it was only once  mikusu rejected him that he fully  committed to being Chad Aaron and that's  because after this rejection he felt  that his only remaining option was to do  the rambling and to do the rambling it  was practical to adopt this detached  Persona if Mika said had given him the  answer he wanted to hear then we all  know he would have ran away with her and  Chad Aaron never would have existed  because that personality was just a  necessary evil that he needed to set the  rumbling in motion it wasn't until the  last chapter that he was finally able to  drop the mask when no one else was  around except Armin and Since Aaron has  nothing more left to lose he just lets  it all out in addition there are two  other reasons why this panel isn't so  bad and the first is that isayama  clearly wanted the scene to have a  comedic element to it evidence not just  by the over-the-top pathetic dialogue  but also by this panel that happened a  second earlier humor is something that  had been almost totally missing because  of the whole Global genocide thing but  with the fighting now completely  finished this was one of the very few  chances to inject a tiny bit of Comedy  before the end the second point is that  underneath the humorous plain to see  that Aaron is suffering here which plays  into one of the main messages of the  series Attack on Titan was super Direct  in pushing the message that genocide is  wrong and so one way of looking at this  panel is that it's a form of punishment  having committed the worst act of  violence in human history it would be  wrong for the story to end with a happy  Aaron being satisfied with the way  things played out instead what we got  was a sad teenager who was scared to die  scared that his crush might forget about  him and who at least acknowledges that  what he did was wrong even if he doesn't  regret it which in the context of this  message was arguably the right thing to  draw with all that said it's time to  switch over to the reasons this panel  doesn't work and I think we need to  begin with Mikasa despite Aaron's love  for her being the main topic of his  meltdown the romance between these two  is something that was massively  underdeveloped the truth is that for 99  of the series Aaron didn't treat Mikasa  like someone he was in love with and  this is something isayama himself was  aware of in an interview he did a couple  of years before the manga ended he said  that for Aaron rather than a lover  mikas's presence is more like a mother  to him the love towards a mother is  considered valuable however at the same  time there are annoying Parts as well as  an audience we also saw for ourselves  that he mostly behaved around her the  same way he did with Armin and their  relationship mostly seemed like one  between family members I know some  people might argue that Aaron was just  too busy with his goals to focus on  romance but even if that's true if he's  in love with her then there would have  been more clues in his behavior to  indicate that was the case in reality  Jean was the one who displayed a more  solid romantic interest in Mikasa  evidenced by him complimenting her looks  getting nervous around her and and  fantasizing about their potential future  in Aaron's case he did virtually none of  that and the closest thing we got was  during the season 2 finale when there  was the chance for a kiss but when the  kiss never materialized it wasn't until  years later the era mentioned anything  remotely romantic Again by that time he  had been avoiding the subject for so  long that mikaso almost didn't know how  to react and despite being in love with  him she gave the answer that was most  likely to preserve their existing  friendship because of that these two  actually being a couple isn't something  that was ever firmly established  especially at this point in the timeline  and so when Aaron melts down about  Mikasa potentially finding another man  it just feels kind of unearned what  makes it even worse is the exact  language he uses for instance when he  says he wants her to be hung up on him  for 10 years at least one thing we need  to understand about all his previous  outbursts is that regardless of the  situation Aaron never stops sounding  like himself like the words he was  saying still sounded right coming from  his mouth with chapter 139 though I'm  struggling to think of a time he's ever  been this level of wine any even when he  was 10 years old I don't think it would  have been this bad as a result the  problem with this moment isn't the fact  that Aaron is having a tantrum but  rather it's the excessively pathetic  dialogue that takes things beyond the  realm of what you'd ever expect to hear  from this character the fact it also  comes at the very end of the mag it  doesn't really help since for most fans  of Aaron it leaves a bad taste in the  mouth for this to be one of the last  things we ever hear him say you could  even argue that although this moment is  meant to be comedic which sort of  justifies it being over the top the  final moments of the main character  isn't really the time to be trying to  get laughs after everything Aaron's been  through and after everything he's done  there's not really anything funny about  this situation and so it's a weird way  to send off one of the most iconic anime  characters all I'm saying is that you  could have had this exact same moment  but with the dialogue being toned down a  bit to make it more believable and less  jokey and I think if that was the case a  lot of people wouldn't have had any  problems of course you still get that  tiny one percent of fans who think that  Aaron is meant to be a Terminator who  doesn't display any real emotion but of  everyone else it would have been so much  easier to read this panel if it had the  same level of believability as his past  Outburst over the years now in terms of  my own personal opinion when the Final  Chapter came out this panel definitely  caught me by surprise in fact for any of  you who haven't seen my original review  my thinking at the time was that this  dialogue was the result of the founder  messing with his head it was easy to  think that because firstly Aaron  basically confirmed it was making him  crazy and secondly the dialogue seemed  so out of character that it felt like  the only rational explanation since then  we've all had more time to think about  it and my thoughts can pretty much be  summarized by answering these three  questions the first being whether I can  see why essayama did it to answer that  I'd say yes I can see why he would want  to do this for all the reasons that we  mentioned in the first half of the video  but if someone was to go back in time  and convince him to write the dialogue  more differently you know more in line  with the whiny errand that we knew then  I think it would have been perfectly  fine like I said before Aaron having a  meltdown is completely Justified  especially because of how repressed he  was so if it was written differently and  I think most reasonable fans wouldn't  have any issue however the reality is  that in its current form I can't say it  was a good thing for this series because  although the meaning of this panel is  clear it's unfortunately let down by the  dialogue and became an iconic moment for  all the wrong reasons that being said  let me know your thoughts about this in  the comments down below do you think  it's fine in its current form or do you  think it should have been changed or  what do you 